Mesa 25.2.8 private build, radeonsi Renoir. System driver unchanged.

Baseline, strict oracle: exit 1; GL_POLYGON LINE x16=0/18.

Experimental NIR GS (single clip-distance component), GL_POLYGON LINE only:
exit 0; x16=18/18, x17=0, x45=18, GL error=0.

Earlier four-component clip-distance export: GPU context lost on first draw;
kernel reported a gfx ring timeout and recovered through reset.

Full oracle with experimental triangle GS: timed out after the quad-line GS;
kernel reported a gfxhub protection fault, a GPU reset, and recovery.
The triangle and point GS paths are disabled in the saved patch. The private
source was rebuilt after that restriction, but the X display disappeared after
the second reset, so this final restricted build was not retested on hardware.

Softpipe private build accepted the generated NIR and completed the strict
oracle, but its unmodified reference already passes, so this is not evidence
that the supplemental Mesa draw is fully correct.
The final restricted build passed the strict oracle on private softpipe under
an isolated Xvfb display. The eight geometry-shader probe cases also passed.
